# mutgap3_res_legacy_heap_leaf_rewrite: An in-process heap (a legacy heap) keeps the transfer buffer its first prepare made (it makes one only when it has none): exec 1 copies a heap buffer out; the guest then moves the heap's first VA page to another RAM page holding other bytes, and exec 2 lists the heap with invalidateHost (flag 1), so it is paged in again from the same buffer, which maps the old RAM page (in the blocks setup the host task's mapping is the old page anyway, memory_gap_table_rewrite): both copies show the old page's bytes. The heap counterpart of mutgap_tex_leaf_rewrite.
